# Nmap Command Notes

## Basic Scan

```bash
nmap 127.0.0.1
```

Scans the 1,000 most common TCP ports on the local machine.

---

## Service Version Detection

```bash
nmap -sV 127.0.0.1
```

Attempts to determine which services are running on open ports and identify their versions.

---

## Full Port Scan

```bash
nmap -p- 127.0.0.1
```

Scans all 65,535 TCP ports.

---

## OS Detection

```bash
sudo nmap -O 127.0.0.1
```

Attempts to detect the operating system.

---

## Useful Concepts

### Localhost

`127.0.0.1` always refers to the current machine.

### Open Port

A program or service is listening on that port.

### Closed Port

The host responds, but no service is listening.

### Filtered Port

A firewall or filtering device prevents Nmap from determining the port state.
